 ## Overview
-Partitioned Volumetric Rendering with RayVolumeIntegral performs volumetric rendering over a partition of possible $t$ values in the union of rendering volumes, combining results from disjoint volume integrals and a void model for empty space [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard single-volume ray marching by explicitly handling multiple disjoint volume bounds and accumulating transmittance across partitions, ensuring correct alpha compositing when rays traverse empty space between volumes [S1, unofficial].
+Partitioned Volumometric Rendering with RayVolumeIntegral performs volumetric rendering over a partition of possible $t$ values in the union of rendering volumes, combining results from disjoint volume integrals and a void model for empty space [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from standard single-volume ray marching by explicitly handling multiple disjoint volume bounds and accumulating transmittance across partitions, ensuring correct alpha compositing when rays traverse empty space between volumes [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Partitioned Volume Rendering Derivation](10384-partitioned-volume-rendering-derivation.md).
 
